    <div class="container">
        <header>
            <h1>Gravitation</h1>
            <p>Chapter 2: Forces and Motion</p>
        </header>

        <main>
            <!-- Section: Introduction -->
            <article class="card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <div class="card-icon">1</div>
                    <div class="card-title">Introduction</div>
                </div>
                <div class="card-content">
                    <p>Gravity is the invisible force that attracts two masses towards each other. It is the force that keeps planets in orbit around the sun and keeps us standing on the Earth. Before Newton, many scientists studied motion, but none had unified the movement of celestial bodies with objects on Earth.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- Section: Definition -->
            <article class="card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <div class="card-icon">2</div>
                    <div class="card-title">Definition</div>
                </div>
                <div class="card-content">
                    <p><strong>Newton’s Law of Universal Gravitation</strong> states that every particle of matter in the universe attracts every other particle with a force that is directly proportional to the product of the masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- Section: Formula (Interactive) -->
            <article class="card formula-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <div class="card-icon">Fx</div>
                    <div class="card-title">The Formula</div>
                </div>
                <div class="card-content">
                    <p>The mathematical expression of this law is:</p>

                    <div class="formula-display">
                        $$ F = G \frac{m_1 m_2}{r^2} $$
                    </div>

                    <div class="formula-actions">
                        <button class="btn-outline" onclick="toggleExplanation()">Explain Formula</button>
                        <button class="btn-primary" onclick="openLab()">Open Formula Lab</button>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Hidden Explanation Area -->
                    <div id="variable-explanation" class="variable-explanation">
                        <div class="var-row">
                            <span class="var-symbol">F</span>
                            <span>Gravitational Force (Newtons)</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="var-row">
                            <span class="var-symbol">G</span>
                            <span>Gravitational Constant ($6.674 \times 10^{-11} \, \text{N}\cdot\text{m}^2/\text{kg}^2$)</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="var-row">
                            <span class="var-symbol">m₁, m₂</span>
                            <span>Masses of the two objects (kg)</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="var-row">
                            <span class="var-symbol">r</span>
                            <span>Distance between the centers of the masses (m)</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>

